<title>GERMANY: DIHT details forecasts for German 1997 exports.</title>
<headline>DIHT details forecasts for German 1997 exports.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German Federation of Chambers of Commerce (DIHT) made the following forecasts for German exports in 1997 (change in percent):</p>
<p>				     1997 (forecast)     1996 (actual)</p>
<p>Exports				   + 6.5	    + 4.6</p>
<p>by region</p>
<p>  Europe				  + 5.5	    + 4.3</p>
<p>   EU members			   + 5		+ 2.8</p>
<p>   Central/eastern Europe	   + 9.5	    + 17.6</p>
<p>  North America (NAFTA)	     + 8.5	    + 9.7</p>
<p>  Latin America (Without Mexico)  + 7		 unch</p>
<p>  Africa				  + 9		- 1.8</p>
<p>  Middle East			   + 7.5	    + 1.7</p>
<p>  Asia/Pacific			  + 9		+ 5.4</p>
<p>NOTE: The DIHT forecasts are based on a survey of German chambers of commerce, delegates and representatives in 75 countries, covering 97 percent of German trade.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
